course: dictionary
lesson: 9477
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning to use. «Its status is contested.» Here, contested means argued over, so status must mean the official position or situation of something, which people do not agree about.
explain: «Jerusalem's status is disputed» uses status in the same way. Disputed means people argue about it, so status is about the city's official position, not a person's rank. Ask yourself: is this word about rank, a situation, or a message? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Status can also mean rank. In history, kings had high status and servants had low status, because of how important people thought they were. The same word can be about a person, a train, or a post online, so always read the clues around it.
fact: Status can mean rank: your position compared with other people, especially how important they think you are.
fact: Status can also mean the situation or condition of something at a certain time, like the status of an order or a train.
fact: A status update is a short message someone posts online about what they are doing or feeling. Think before you post.
fact: «Contested» means argued over, so «Its status is contested» means people do not agree about it.
fact: Phrases to know: social status, status symbol, high status, and «What's the status?»
exercise: In history, kings had high status. What does status mean here? | *Rank, how important you are compared with other people | A short message posted online | A kind of bird | The colour of a flag
exercise: «Its status is contested.» What does contested mean? | Very quick and easy | *Argued over, so people do not agree | Finished and settled for good | Painted bright red
exercise: Mia says her train's status is «delayed». What does status mean here? | Her rank in the class | A message she posted online | *The situation of the train at a certain time | Her legal position as a citizen
test: Which meaning fits «Jerusalem's status is disputed»? | *Its official position, which people argue about | A short post about the city online | Its height above the sea | How many people live in the city
test: What is a status update? | *A short message someone posts online about what they are doing or feeling | A rank given to a king | A long letter sent through the post | A timetable for trains
exam: Which sentence uses status to mean rank? | The status of the flight is delayed. | Her status update was funny. | *Servants in the old days had low status. | Its status is contested.
